&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="page-break-after: avoid; border: none; mso-padding-alt: 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt; mso-border-shadow: yes;"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: black;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;font style="mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: black;"&gt;At June&amp;#160;30, 2026, OG&amp;amp;E was in compliance with all of its debt agreements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
